"""conduit-ctl-agent: the Linux guest end of Conduit's control channel.

The host talks to the guest over the virtio-serial port `org.conduit.ctl.0`
(guest side: /dev/virtio-ports/org.conduit.ctl.0): one JSON object per line
in, one per line out. The protocol is host/ctl/src/lib.rs; the operations are
ping, run, stop, apps, icon, put, get and ls.

The agent runs as a systemd user service (or XDG autostart entry) in the
user's desktop session, so everything it does is done as that user. Python 3
standard library only. Never dies on a bad request: every request is answered,
with `{"id":N,"ok":false,"error":"..."}` when it fails.
"""

